T (Task):
My goal was to ensure full manual and automated test coverage for this module, even as its features were being developed and
released incrementally. There were no existing automation patterns or reusable components for this part of the application.

A (Action):
I started by manually mapping out the user flows and identifying key integration points between features.
For automation, I initially used static selectors, but frequent UI changes made maintenance difficult.
I adapted by implementing robust, dynamic selectors and modular test functions that could easily be updated as the UI evolved.
 I also created utility methods for common actions across sub-features, which improved efficiency and consistency.

R (Result):
This approach allowed me to maintain stable and scalable automation scripts, even as the module changed rapidly.
The framework I built enabled quick onboarding of new features and was later leveraged by the team for other modules.
As a result, we achieved reliable test coverage and supported timely releases without major setbacks.

